ngs, committee work, advises students academically, holds regular office hours, and assists with College events, service to the College, and other activities. Mount Aloysius College offers a generous benefits package for full-time employees including but not limited to: medical/health, dental, vision, and life insurance; short-term and long-term disability insurance; Retirement plan match; tuition remission; and an employee assistance program, among others. Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) required.  Doctorate preferred (PhD, DNP, EdD) earned or in final semester/ABD with pending graduation date.  Two (2) to three (3) years of leadership experience in nursing education administration required.  Prior classroom and clinical teaching experience at the collegiate level required. Valid, unencumbered license as a registered nurse or advanced practice nurse in Pennsylvania required. Minimum 3-4 years of nursing experience, with at least two years in behavioral health nursing and a demonstrated ability to perform at a high level is required. A strong student focus is required, with the ability to relay information effectively.  Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected.  Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and demonstrate the ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office.  High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. Proficiency in curriculum design, evaluation, instruction, program administration, and academic advising also preferred.  Faculty rank is dependent upon education, experience and credentials. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College’s Expansion into DuBois, PA Mo